    "q-218745": {
      "dom_id": "step-q218745",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "What is the solution to the following system of inequalities?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3t-2<-8 \\\\ t+1<-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution is\n$t$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To solve the system, we need to find the values of $t$ that satisfy both $3t-2<-8$ and $t+1<-2$ simultaneously.\n\n- First, we solve $3t-2<-8\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3t-2 & <-8 \\\\ 3t-2+2 & <-8+2 \\\\ 3t & <-6 \\\\ \\frac{3t}{3} & <\\frac{-6}{3} \\\\ t & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/b97b78ec613e826f7f8beb7336d3c2f285fc58d9bbf0c0f9d59921f41de2b3b6.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $t+1<-2\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t+1 & <-2 \\\\ t+1-1 & <-2-1 \\\\ t & <-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/cfb26921afb706908f771e1934cf27c0ca6e248e9e3aca54f499af685393fa86.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $t$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/6d488376420476cf34798aeb3fced46770a177288b550f2e887348c582741321.png)\n\n \n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nThus, the final solution is $t<-3.$",
