    "q-76004": {
      "dom_id": "step-q76004",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $4x+9\\ge 1$ and $1-3x>7.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve the system, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $4x+9\\ge 1\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+9 & \\ge 1 \\\\ 4x+9-9 & \\ge 1-9 \\\\ 4x & \\ge -8 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & \\ge \\frac{-8}{4} \\\\ x & \\ge -2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/1673c69df6497fd90ddab9c51c208ca5110f0e3c5a03a101e3b46723e04081fe.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve $1-3x>7\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-3x & >7 \\\\ 1-3x-1 & >7-1 \\\\ -3x & >6 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-3x) & <(-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\ 3x & <-6 \\\\ \\frac{3x}{3} & <\\frac{-6}{3} \\\\ x & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/b97b78ec613e826f7f8beb7336d3c2f285fc58d9bbf0c0f9d59921f41de2b3b6.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/544d23551ed218c0d7e373ba0d04dbe1ad51d587c452b875c1a45df2e896cd87.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIt turns out that the solutions do not overlap at all. Therefore, there are no values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities simultaneously. So, there is no solution.",
